From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kodi-iris contributors <kodi-iris@invalid>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 12:58:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] hevcdec: refuse >8-bit streams at open when DRM_PRIME is
 preset

Kodi's DRMPRIME codec retries with the software decoder after a hardware
decoder refuses a stream, presetting pix_fmt=DRM_PRIME; its get_format only
accepts 8-bit software formats, so 10-bit HEVC failed on every frame (black
screen).  Failing avcodec_open2 makes Kodi fall back to its plain FFmpeg
software decoder, which handles 10-bit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 libavcodec/hevc/hevcdec.c | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libavcodec/hevc/hevcdec.c b/libavcodec/hevc/hevcdec.c
index a625d3ab88..f11e4f6af4 100644
--- a/libavcodec/hevc/hevcdec.c
+++ b/libavcodec/hevc/hevcdec.c
@@ -4201,11 +4201,30 @@ static av_cold int hevc_decode_init(AVCodecContext *avctx)
         const AVPacketSideData *sd;
 
         if (avctx->extradata_size > 0 && avctx->extradata) {
+            /* A caller that presets DRM_PRIME on this software decoder (Kodi's
+             * DRMPRIME path after a hardware decoder refused the stream) can
+             * only take 8-bit software formats.  Refuse >8-bit streams at open
+             * so the caller falls back to its plain software decoder instead
+             * of failing every frame in get_format. */
+            const int want_drm_prime = avctx->pix_fmt == AV_PIX_FMT_DRM_PRIME;
+
             ret = hevc_decode_extradata(s, avctx->extradata, avctx->extradata_size, 1);
             if (ret < 0) {
                 return ret;
             }
 
+            if (want_drm_prime) {
+                for (int i = 0; i < FF_ARRAY_ELEMS(s->ps.sps_list); i++) {
+                    const HEVCSPS *sps = s->ps.sps_list[i];
+                    if (sps && sps->bit_depth > 8) {
+                        av_log(avctx, AV_LOG_INFO,
+                               "DRM_PRIME requested but stream is %d-bit: refusing\n",
+                               sps->bit_depth);
+                        return AVERROR(ENOSYS);
+                    }
+                }
+            }
+
             ret = hevc_sei_to_context(avctx, &s->sei);
             if (ret < 0)
                 return ret;
